[
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_BERSERK_WYALD_MUSTER_ROLL",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "The lists separate soldiers, prisoners and those taken to the leader. Human boot sizes and ration counts fill the early pages. Later marks describe warped guards wearing the same uniforms. This was an army before its cruelty took a monstrous shape. The broken wagon lies west of the tents; the quarry leaves a southern way around the cages.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_BERSERK_WYALD_PRISONER_ACCOUNT",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "I hid this before they counted us. The cage doors are tied, not locked with iron keys. Untie them from either side and pass through; the quarry is longer but stays open. The bells in the wagon can ring after you leave. Do not stand there waiting, and do not believe the leader will stop hunting because he hears them. One name at the bottom is followed by a small word: escaped.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_BERSERK_WYALD_COMMAND_ORDERS",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "Wyald ordered the stolen stores counted and the fighting ground cleared. Timber screens were dragged to its edges; three wrecked barriers remain on the open earth. Leave space beside them for a sidestep when he braces to charge. The last order names a world broken open: his old fate was diverted by the crossing, and the being leading this camp is alive, not an echo.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_BERSERK_ROSINE_WITNESS_NOTE",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "They called the winged things fairies because the flowers were beautiful. I followed their lost shoes past the games to the silk. The still shells were empty of hope; the moving ones held something already changed. Break a swelling cocoon before it opens and no creature will fly out of that shell. I cannot bring the transformed back. The shallow western gully bends around the grove toward the great roots.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "effect_on_condition",
    "id": "EOC_BERSERK_READ_BERSERK_ROSINE_FADED_RIBBON",
    "effect": {
      "u_message": "The ribbon was tied around a twig as a marker in a game. Another knot is clenched inside a split shell farther along. The flowers kept growing when the games stopped. This little thing records a person, not a treasure hidden in a creature.",
      "type": "info",
      "popup": true
    }
  },
